<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qian'an</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qian'an is a county-level city in Tangshan prefecture, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the Luan River near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-wall-of-china">Great Wall</a>. In the late 3rd and early 4th centuries the area was the base of the Duan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a>, whose seat at Lingzhi lay nearby. It is now a centre of iron mining and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> production.</p></div>
